# SRG-APP-000795-WSR-000130  -  CAT II
# The web server must alert organization-defined personnel or roles upon
# detection of unauthorized access, modification, or deletion of audit
# information.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000795-WSR-000130
group:           V-264340
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-003831
control_rev5:    AU-9

contribution:    Splunk Web is a component of the application rather than a separate web
                 server, and the alerting surface serving this objective is the same saved
                 search and email action; the application names the Splunk Web access log
                 that supplies the detection source and holds the alert and its recipient
                 list.

governs:         alert_actions.conf - What Splunk does when an alert fires, such as sending email or calling a
                 webhook.
governs:         savedsearches.conf - Saved searches, scheduled reports and alerts.
governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] action.email in 1|true
check:           savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] action.email.to non_empty
check:           alert_actions.conf [email] present
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] alert_condition https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/savedsearches.conf
vendor:          web.conf [settings] log.access_file https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
vendor:          web.conf [settings] startwebserver https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
retired_check:   web.conf [settings] startwebserver equals 1
                 reason: "startwebserver = [0 | 1]. Set whether or not to start Splunk Web.
                         0 disables Splunk Web, 1 enables it. Default: 1"
retired_check:   web.conf [settings] log.access_file non_empty
                 reason: "log.access_file = <filename>. The HTTP access log filename. This
                         file is written in the default $SPLUNK_HOME/var/log directory.
                         Default: web_access.log" Related shipped settings:
                         log.access_maxsize = 25000000 and log.access_maxfiles = 5.
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The personnel or roles to notify are an organization-defined parameter the
                 application can hold but not determine.
external:        Delivery of the notification rests on the mail transfer agent and the
                 network.
external:        The Splunk Web access record must be monitored into an index for an alert
                 to evaluate it; where that input is configured on another instance, that
                 instance's configuration carries the remainder.
external:        Product STIG SPLK-CL-000140 carries the related personnel element - admin
                 role membership matching the ISSM's list - through the directory service
                 group mapped to the admin role and an ISSM-maintained roster, neither of
                 which is an application setting.
external:        Which saved search carries the trigger, which is organization-defined
                 content: a trigger is expressed either by alert_condition or by counttype
                 with relation and quantity, so a test on alert_condition alone reports a
                 finding against a search that is correctly configured the other way.

citation:        web.conf.spec:16 [settings], :23 startwebserver = [0 | 1] default 1, :871
                 log.access_file default web_access.log; savedsearches.conf.spec:270
                 alert_condition, :300 action.email, :304 action.email.to;
                 alert_actions.conf.spec:157 [email]. Product STIG SPLK-CL-000140.
finding:         Assessed at the application layer alone: Splunk Web names no access log,
                 or no saved search carries a trigger condition over unauthorized access,
                 modification or deletion of that audit information with a notification
                 action and a recipient list.
